<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1594">1594</a>–<a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim was a Bavarian-born field marshal of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. A convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>, he became famous as a bold cavalry commander, took part in the sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> in 1631 and was mortally wounded at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutzen-1632">Lützen</a> in 1632. He was the best-known member of the hereditary marshals of Pappenheim.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim.jpg" alt="Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gottfried_Henrich_von_Pappenheim-Treuchtlingen,_1594-1632_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15460.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
